https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-03-28T17:19:53Z","updated_at":"2019-03-28T17:29:48Z","body":"similar failure with this code with no import:\r\n```python3\r\n# context\r\nclass MetaA(type):\r\n    pass\r\nclass A(metaclass=MetaA):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\nclass MetaB(type):\r\n    pass\r\nclass B(metaclass=MetaB):\r\n    pass\r\n```\r\nthe following inheritance fails with pylint:\r\n```python3\r\nclass C(A, B, metaclass=type('', (type(A), type(B)), {})):\r\n    pass\r\n```\r\n=>\r\n```\r\ninternal error with sending report for module ['test.py']\r\nDuplicates found in MROs (), (type, object), (type, object), (type, type) for <ClassDef l.11 at 0x7fbdc3bd4d68>.\r\n```\r\nbut surprisingly, with a variable, the almost same code is working:\r\n```python3\r\nMetaC = type('', (type(A), type(B)), {})\r\nclass C(A, B, metaclass=MetaC):\r\n    pass\r\n```\r\nversion:\r\n```\r\npylint 2.3.1\r\nastroid 2.2.5\r\nPython 3.5.3 (default, Sep 27 2018, 17:25:39) \r\n[GCC 6.3.0 20170516]\r\n```\r\nthe output of the error is the same as #2666 and #2754\r\n\r\nedit: related to https://github.com/PyCQA/astroid/issues/633 and https://github.com/PyCQA/astroid/pull/634","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/477691794/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"SamyCookie","id":2362591,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNjI1OTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2362591?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie","html_url":"https://github.com/SamyCookie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamyCookie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/483495023","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/2443#issuecomment-483495023","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/2443","id":483495023,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4MzQ5NTAyMw==","user":{"login":"brycepg","id":441800,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MTgwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/441800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg","html_url":"https://github.com/brycepg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-04-16T03:14:52Z","updated_at":"2019-04-16T04:06:25Z","body":"Thanks @SamyCookie for digging into this futher. I can reproduce this with just astroid now.\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport astroid\r\n\r\nnode = astroid.extract_node(\"\"\"\r\n# context\r\nclass MetaA(type):\r\n    pass\r\nclass A(metaclass=MetaA):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\nclass MetaB(type):\r\n    pass\r\nclass B(metaclass=MetaB):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\nclass C(metaclass=type('', (type(A), type(B)), {})):\r\n    pass\r\nC #@\r\n\"\"\").inferred()[0]\r\nmetaclass = node.declared_metaclass()\r\nmetaclass.mro() # DuplicateBasesError here\r\n```\r\n\r\nSpecifically, the error occurs because the astroid detects duplicate bases of `type`.\r\n\r\nastroid detects duplicate bases of `type` because it's inferring the the `bases` of the metaclass to be `type` and `type` and not the `MetaA` and `MetaB`, but only when constructed through the declared_metaclass call.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis appears to be a bug in `Call` inference inside the metaclass keyword because the following change does not trigger the issue (The ta base properly infers to `MetaA`):\r\n\r\n```python\r\nta = type(A)\r\nclass C(metaclass=type('', (ta, type(B)), {})):\r\n    pass\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/483495023/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"brycepg","id":441800,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MTgwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/441800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg","html_url":"https://github.com/brycepg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"http